# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository.
#
# Rationale: the repo had no line-ending normalization while core.autocrlf=true,
# so files were stored CRLF on disk and airbnb-base's `linebreak-style: ['error','lf']`
# flagged ~324k spurious problems (98% of all ESLint output). See
# docs/ARCHITECTURAL_REVIEW.md §2.5 and docs/ARCHITECTURAL_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md Phase 0.
#
# After this file is committed, run ONCE (as its own dedicated commit, on a clean
# working tree) to convert already-tracked files:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "chore: normalize line endings to LF"

* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that the OS requires in a specific ending.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize or diff these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.glb   binary
*.gltf  binary
*.ktx2  binary
*.basis binary
*.hdr   binary
*.exr   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.node  binary
*.wasm  binary
